.TH SDL_AudioStreamDevicePaused 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_AudioStreamDevicePaused \- Use this function to query if an audio device associated with a stream is paused.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_AudioStreamDevicePaused(SDL_AudioStream *stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlike in SDL2, audio devices start in an _unpaused_ state, since an app has to bind a stream before any audio will flow\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I stream
the audio stream associated with the audio device to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if device is valid and paused, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_PauseAudioStreamDevice (3),
.BR SDL_ResumeAudioStreamDevice (3)
